    "teacher_markdown": "# VibeCheck's \"For You\" Page\r\n\r\nUse the CHAT Framework to update the basic functionality of VibeCheck's \"For You\" page.\r\n\r\nPossibilities for students: \r\n\r\n### 1. Clarify\r\n* Inspect the data in the code, and choose filtering and sorting \r\n    * *Popularity?* Sort by `likes`.\r\n    * *Virality?* Sort by `shares`.\r\n    * *Clickbait?* Sort by `views`.\r\n\r\n### 2. Hone / Apply (Build the Filter)\r\nE.g. - Remove the noise (posts older than 24 hours).\r\n* Create `filterRecent(data)` and a new empty array `recentPosts`.\r\n* Use `.map()` to loop through `data`.\r\n* **If** `post.hoursAgo < 24`, **push** the post to `recentPosts`.\r\n* Return the `recentPosts` array.\r\n\r\n### 3. Hone / Apply (Build the Sorter)\r\nRank the content using your chosen metric.\r\n* Create `rankByValues(data)`.\r\n* Call `data.sort()`.\r\n* Inside the sort function `(a, b)`, subtract your chosen field (e.g., `b.shares - a.shares`) to sort descending.\r\n\r\n### 4. Apply & Test\r\nConnect the pipeline at the bottom:\r\n1.  Call `filterRecent` -> save to variable.\r\n2.  Call `rankByValues` on that variable.\r\n3.  Call `renderFeed` to see if your unique algorithm works!",
    "display_name": "\"For You\" Feed",
    "bubble_choice_description": "You have been hired to fix the \"For You\" feed for a new video app called **VibeCheck**.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/1e897361cb01ce52a56dfe980fa2ca90-tiktok.jpg"
  },
  "published": true,
